From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] viogpu3d: immediate flips through SetVidPnSourceAddress too

The driver flipped only on vsync by MMIO (FlipOnVSyncMmIo). A flip with sync interval 0 (a full-screen swap chain
presenting without vsync, as 3DMark Vantage's tests do) Windows then makes a DMA buffer flip, which Present
doesn't do: the frames never reached the display, which kept the tests' loading screen (ETW: Flip events with
MMIOFlip false). FlipImmediateMmIo has those flips go through SetVidPnSourceAddress as well. Not on Windows 7, whose
WDDM 1.1 caps don't have it.
---
--- a/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_adapter.cpp
+++ b/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_adapter.cpp
@@ -680,6 +680,12 @@
                 pDriverCaps->HighestAcceptableAddress.QuadPart = (ULONG64)-1;
 
                 pDriverCaps->FlipCaps.FlipOnVSyncMmIo = TRUE;
+#if !VIOGPU_WIN7
+                // Immediate flips (sync interval 0) through SetVidPnSourceAddress as well: without it Windows made them
+                // DMA buffer flips, which Present doesn't do, and a full-screen game presenting so never reached the
+                // display (3DMark Vantage's tests showed their loading screen)
+                pDriverCaps->FlipCaps.FlipImmediateMmIo = TRUE;
+#endif
 
                 pDriverCaps->MaxQueuedFlipOnVSync = 1;
 
